      <div class="data-point">Data Point: Product defect mentions ('broken', 'defective', 'not working') rank among top 10 negative themes</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rec-card">
      <h4>5. Curate the Catalog for Quality — {high_rating_pct:.0f}% High-Rating Share Is a Starting Point</h4>
      <p>While {high_rating_pct:.1f}% of products rate 4.0+, the remaining {(100-high_rating_pct):.1f}% represent an opportunity. Set a target to increase high-rating share to 85%+ through delisting consistently low-rated products and promoting high-rated alternatives. Create a "Customer Favorites" curation featuring products in the 4.5+ rating tier with significant review counts.</p>
      <div class="data-point">Data Point: {high_rating_pct:.1f}% of products currently rated ≥ 4.0; {(df_valid['rating_num'] >= 4.5).mean()*100:.1f}% rated ≥ 4.5</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</div><!-- /container -->

<div class="report-footer">
  <p>Amazon Product Catalog Performance &amp; Customer Sentiment Analysis &mdash; Data sourced from Amazon India product catalog (Kaggle) &mdash; {len(df):,} products analyzed &mdash; Generated May 2026</p>
</div>

</body>
</html>'''

# ── Write output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
os.makedirs('/app/output', exist_ok=True)
with open(OUTPUT_PATH, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write(html)

file_size = os.path.getsize(OUTPUT_PATH)
print(f"\nReport written to {OUTPUT_PATH}")
print(f"File size: {file_size:,} bytes ({file_size/1024:.1f} KB)")

# ── Validate: verify data integrity ────────────────────────────────────────
print("\n── Validation ──")
print(f"  Total products: {total_products}")
print(f"  Valid rated products: {len(df_valid)}")
print(f"  Missing ratings: {df['rating_num'].isna().sum()}")
print(f"  Top categories: {df_valid['top_category'].nunique()}")
print(f"  Avg rating range: {df_valid['rating_num'].min():.2f} - {df_valid['rating_num'].max():.2f}")
print(f"  Discount range: {df['discount_pct_num'].min():.1f}% - {df['discount_pct_num'].max():.1f}%")
print(f"  Price range: ₹{df['discounted_price_num'].min():,.0f} - ₹{df['discounted_price_num'].max():,.0f}")

# Check all KPIs are from data
print(f"  Correlation verified: discount-rating r={discount_rating_corr:.4f}")
print(f"  Correlation verified: price-rating r={price_rating_corr:.4f}")
